<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">George Bowen</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1821–1899</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">George Bowen was a British colonial governor who became the first governor of Queensland when it separated from New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/south-wales">South Wales</a> in 1859. He later governed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/new-zealand">New Zealand</a>, Victoria, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mauritius">Mauritius</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hong-kong">Hong Kong</a>. In Queensland he presided over rapid pastoral expansion and the setting up of the colony's parliament.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/george-bowen.jpg" alt="George Bowen" width="320" height="391" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unidentified · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:George_Bowen_b.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
